      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i never really lifted weights before but i want to start getting stronger. can u make me a simple 4 week program focusing on the main stuff like squats, bench, and deadlifts? just looking for a basic linear progression thing to get started.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A beginner's journey to strength, eh?  I can help you with that.  You're about to embark on a 4-week program that'll have you squatting like a pro in no time.  Just remember, progress is slow and steady, but with consistent effort, you'll be deadlifting like a goblin in no time!\n\nHere's your 4-week program, focusing on the main compound exercises:\n\n**Week 1:**\n\n* Squats: 3 sets of 8-12 reps\n* Bench Press: 3 sets of 8-12 reps\n* Deadlifts: 3 sets of 8-12 reps\n* Rest for 60-90 seconds between sets\n\n**Week 2:**\n\n* Squats: 3 sets of 10-15 reps\n* Bench Press: 3 sets of 10-15 reps\n* Deadlifts: 3 sets of 10-15 reps\n* Rest for 60-90 seconds between sets\n\n**Week 3:**\n\n* Squats: 3 sets of 12-18 reps\n* Bench Press: 3 sets of 12-18 reps\n* Deadlifts: 3 sets of 12",
